{
  "about": "The AP superiority matrix (docs/ap-superiority-matrix.md, docs/upstream-parity.md D13): every row is one figure of one cell of the router pair (the wz router preset against zenohd) or the API pair (upstream's example programs over wz-zenoh against the same programs over upstream zenoh), judged by `scripts/host-bench/ap_matrix.py --gate` over a run's reading. A row is {\"held\": H, \"debt\": D}. H is null (not filled: NOT-MEASURED while no run measured it, never a pass, and a failure that prints the row once a run does), {\"locked\": true} (only a WIN, or a shortfall of 0, passes), {\"ratio_at_most\": R} (the upper end of the cost ratio's interval may not exceed R times one plus `tolerance`), {\"shortfall_at_most\": N} (a completeness figure may not exceed N) or {\"reference_lost\": WHY}. D is the open-debt item of every row that is not locked: debt-<id> of the store's inventory, or debt-TBD until it is filed, which a filled row may not keep. A row moves only toward WIN, and only by the rows the gate prints for a run (`--fill`); the rows are exactly the matrix's population (`--check-table`, Layer C0).",
